/-!
# Vanishing of sheaf cohomology from Čech vanishing on a cofinal system of coverings

Let `C` be a site and let `B` be a collection of objects of `C`. Suppose given, for each
object `U`, a collection of coverings of `U`, such that the coverings selected for the
objects of `B` are cofinal among all coverings of those objects, and such that every object
appearing in one of those coverings — the members of the covering and all of their nonempty
finite fibre products — again lies in `B`. Stacks 03F9 asserts that an abelian sheaf `F`
whose positive-degree Čech cohomology vanishes on all the selected coverings has vanishing
positive-degree sheaf cohomology on every object of `B`.

The proof is the induction of the source. For `n = 1` one embeds `F` in an injective abelian
sheaf `I` with cokernel `Q`; Stacks 03F8 turns the degree-one Čech vanishing for `F` into
surjectivity of `I → Q` on sections over every object of `B`, and the long exact sequence
for `Ext` out of the free abelian sheaf on an object then kills `H¹(U, F)`. The same
surjectivity makes the Čech complexes of `F`, `I` and `Q` on a selected covering into a
short exact sequence of complexes; since the Čech cohomology of the injective sheaf `I`
vanishes in positive degrees, the long exact sequence of that short exact sequence of
complexes transfers the Čech vanishing hypothesis from `F` to `Q`, with a degree shift. The
inductive hypothesis applied to `Q` in degree `n` and the `Ext` sequence again then give the
vanishing in degree `n + 1` for `F`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.CechSite.sheafCohomology_isZero_of_cechCohomology_isZero_of_enoughInjectives`: the
  Čech-vanishing criterion for the vanishing of sheaf cohomology on a collection of objects of
  a site, with the homological inputs of the proof as hypotheses rather than smallness.
* `Stacks.CechSite.sheafCohomology_isZero_of_cechCohomology_isZero`: the same criterion for a
  site small in the coefficient universe, which is the form of the source.

## Implementation notes

A covering of `U` is a `PreZeroHypercover U`, as in Stacks 03AM, whose generated sieve
belongs to the Grothendieck topology, so the selected coverings form a dependent family of
sets of such subtypes. Cofinality says that the sieve generated by some selected covering is
contained in any given covering sieve. A Grothendieck topology supplies no chosen fibre
products, so their existence for the selected coverings is a hypothesis, and a further
hypothesis says that the chosen products lie in `B`. Both Čech and sheaf-cohomology
vanishing are expressed by `CategoryTheory.Limits.IsZero`.

The selected coverings have an independent index universe `w`; the coefficient and morphism
universes are enlarged together to `max v w` so as to contain those indices, without
identifying the universe of objects with either of them. The source excludes big categories
as sites (Sites, Remark 00VI), so `Small.{max v w} C` is assumed; this is what gives enough
injective abelian sheaves, by passage to a small model of the site, as the source's proof
and its definition of sheaf cohomology require (Injectives, Theorem 01DP).

Positive-degree Čech vanishing for an injective abelian presheaf, Stacks 03OR, is reproved
here as the private `injective_cechCohomology_isZero'` because the object universe is left
unrelated to the coefficient universe: the exact `Hom` functor is applied to the integral
Čech complex of Stacks 03AS and 03AT, and exactness is reflected through coefficient
universe lifting, which is possible because the coefficients already contain the morphism
and covering-index universes.

